@FOOTNOTE{Note1,key="Note1",note="In backward SBS the written phonon grating extends over the signal--pump collision length, $L_c\approx 0.26$~m for 3-ns signal and 1-ns pump pulses, not over an acoustic wavelength. For a 10-GHz bin spacing the phase mismatch between bins is $\Delta q\approx 964$~rad/m, so $\Delta q\protect \,L_c\approx 251$ and different bins write mutually orthogonal gratings. In our one-dimensional space--time simulation of a two-bin, mode-selective write, the selectivity between the targeted and the orthogonal bin superposition drops to 0.5, i.e.\ no selectivity. The scheme would also need meter-scale interaction lengths ($\approx $1.3~m for 100-MHz photons) and watt-level pump power ($P_\pi \approx 1.55$~W at 100~MHz). These are our estimates from TFLN literature parameters and have not been tested experimentally."}
